<H2><FONT COLOR="#D60021">5.6.1.5.</FONT></H2>
</TD>
<TD VALIGN=top>
<H2>Model Selection Criterion</H2>
</TD>
</TR >
</TABLE>
</TD>
</TR>







<!-- begin paragraph -->
<TR>
<TD WIDTH=15% VALIGN=top>
<!-- Add marginal notes below -->
<I>
Criterion for Including Terms in the Model
</I>
</TD>
<TD WIDTH=85% VALIGN=top>
<!-- Add main text below -->
There are several criterion that we can use in determining which terms
to include in our model.
<OL>
   <LI><img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/absbeta.gif">
       &nbsp;>&nbsp; the minimum engineering significant
       <img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/delta.gif">
       <P>
   <LI>look for natural spacing and gaps in the 
       <img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/absbeta.gif">
       <P>
   <LI><img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/absbeta2.gif">
       <P>
   <LI><img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/absbeta3.gif">
       <P>
       where <img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/sigma.gif">
       can be estimated from:
       <OL>
          <LI>An a priori engineering judgement.
          <LI>The data if replication is present.
          <LI>The standard deviation of the residuals if we
              ignore all 3-term and higher interactions.
          <LI>The <img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/sdbeta.gif">
              are estimated from a simple standard deviation 
              calculated from all
              <img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/betaijk.gif">
              from 3-term interactions and higher.
       </OL>
       <P>
   <LI>A <a href="../../eda/section3/normprpl.htm">normal probability
       plot</a> of
       <img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/betahat.gif">.
       <P>
   <LI>A halfnormal
       <a href="../../eda/section3/probplot.htm">probability plot</a>
       of <img align=absmiddle src="splett3/eqns/absbeta.gif">.
       <P>
   <LI>A <a href="../../eda/section3/youdplot.htm">Youden plot</a>
       of the factor means.
       <P>
   <LI>The cumulative residual standard deviaition is less than
       the minimum engineering residual standard deviation.
</OL>

</TD>
</TR>
<!-- end paragraph -->

<!-- begin paragraph -->
<TR>
<TD WIDTH=15% VALIGN=top>
<!-- Add marginal notes below -->
<A NAME="normprob">
<I>
Normal Probablity Plot of Effects and Halfnormal Probability
Plot of Effects
</I>
</A>
</TD>
<TD WIDTH=85% VALIGN=TOP>
<!-- Add main text below -->
The following plot shows the normal probability plot of the
effects and the halfnormal probability plot of the absolute value
of the effects.
<P>
<A HREF="splett3/gifs/normpr_f.gif">
<img src="splett3/gifs/normpr_r.gif"
     HEIGHT=425 WIDTH=550 BORDER=0
     alt="probability plots indicate that model should include main effects for factor 1 and factor 2 with no interaction terms">
</A>
<P>
The halfnormal probability plot indicates that we should include main
effect terms for factor 1 and factor 2 with no interaction terms.
The normal probability plot is more ambiguous.  Although the factor 1
main effect term clearly stands out, the next 5 terms line up in
a fairly linear fashion.

</TD>
</TR>
<!-- end paragraph -->

<!-- begin paragraph -->
<TR>
<TD WIDTH=15% VALIGN=top>
<!-- Add marginal notes below -->
<A NAME="youden">
<I>
Youden Plot of Effects
</I>
</A>
</TD>
<TD WIDTH=85%>
<!-- Add main text below -->
The following is the Youden plot of the effects.
<P>
<A HREF="splett3/gifs/youden_f.gif">
<img src="splett3/gifs/youden_r.gif"
     HEIGHT=425 WIDTH=550 BORDER=0
     alt="Youden plot show factor 1 and factor 2 main effects stand out">
</A>
<P>
The Youden plot of the effects shows that the main effects for
factor 1 and factor 2 stand out.

</TD>
</TR>
<!-- end paragraph -->




   
